Offline AI Chatbot using Phi-3 and Ollama
1️⃣ Introduction

The project includes an AI chatbot that works completely offline.
The chatbot uses a local Large Language Model (LLM) to understand user questions and generate responses.

Instead of using online AI services, the chatbot runs on the local computer using Ollama and the Phi-3 language model.

This allows the chatbot to:

Answer questions

Assist users with course information

Provide guidance without internet access

The model Phi-3 was developed by Microsoft.

2️⃣ What is Ollama?

Ollama is a tool that allows developers to run large AI language models locally on their computer.

Main Features

Runs AI models offline

Easy to install and use

Provides an API for Python applications

Supports many AI models

Examples of models supported:

Phi-3

Llama

Mistral

In this project, Phi-3 is used as the chatbot model.

3️⃣ What is Phi-3?

Phi-3 is a small but powerful language model created by Microsoft.

It belongs to the field of
Natural Language Processing (NLP).

Purpose

Phi-3 can:

Understand human language

Answer questions

Generate text

Assist users in conversations

Advantages

Lightweight model

Fast response

Works well on normal computers

Can run completely offline

4️⃣ Installing Ollama

Step 1
Download Ollama from the official website.

Step 2
Install the software.

Step 3
Check installation by opening terminal or command prompt and running:

ollama --version

If installed correctly, it will show the version number.

5️⃣ Downloading the Phi-3 Model

Run this command in terminal:

ollama run phi3

The first time you run this command:

Ollama downloads the Phi-3 model

The model is saved locally on your computer

After downloading, it can run without internet.

6️⃣ How the Chatbot Works

System workflow:

User Input
     ↓
Python Application
     ↓
Ollama Local API
     ↓
Phi-3 AI Model
     ↓
Generated Response
     ↓
Displayed to User

The chatbot reads the user’s question and sends it to the Phi-3 model running locally.

The model processes the question and returns an answer.

7️⃣ Python Integration

The chatbot is connected to Ollama using Python.

Example Python code:

import requests

url = "http://localhost:11434/api/generate"

data = {
    "model": "phi3",
    "prompt": "What is machine learning?",
    "stream": False
}

response = requests.post(url, json=data)

print(response.json()["response"])
Explanation

Python sends a request to Ollama

Ollama sends the prompt to the Phi-3 model

The model generates an answer

The response is returned to Python

